# Dynamic array rejects an incompatible typed boundary

Verifies statically known heterogeneous contents are rejected before a dynamic
array can enter an integer-array contract.

>>> source
let source = [1, "two", 3]
let values: int[] = source

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: dynamic array does not satisfy `int64[]` at Span { start: 47, end: 53 }

<<< exit
1
